# `band_span_charge` default-flip vehicle (issue #518) — HEALED, at a WL cost.
# This flow and flow/rnr/mix2.buda are the two corpus vehicles the flip cost.
# History: 0/0/0 pre-flip -> 3/16/1 at the flip (#527/#530) -> 16 opens healed
# by #531/#534, leaving 3 overlaps (issue #535) -> 1 overlap by 2026-08-02 (a
# free ride from later planner/healer work) -> 0/0/0 now, via the trailing
# `chase_overlaps` refine documented at the end of this script.  The residual
# root cause was the absolute-supply blind spot: the width books say the
# spread bus fits, but DetailedNUTS still needs real SIGNAL tracks at the
# placed position.  See docs/internal/band_span_charge.md.
#
# Uncomment before run_planner to restore the PRE-FLIP endpoint on this flow:
#set_planner_param band_span_charge 0
#
# Deliberately NOT applied: this is a corpus row, and silencing the charging
# model would make the QoR guard stop reporting its known real cost.  The
# `chase_overlaps` fix below is NOT that — it leaves band_span_charge at its
# default and pays the cost visibly in wirelength instead of in overlaps.
#
# Selection-basis lever 3 composition vehicle (the refine_selection docs
# recipe, measured 2026-07-30): the PLAIN top-down mix2 pipeline (no healers)
# ends at 175 DNUTS opens / 16 NUTS overlaps on the reference x86 build; the
# end-of-flow recipe
#   refine_selection -> negotiate_congestion -> ripup_reroute -> refine_selection
# heals it to a fully clean check_design (0 opens / 0 overlaps, Success):
# refine's componentwise pre-shrink (175->84 opens, WL 67558->65480) hands the
# healers a much smaller problem, negotiate cracks the residual (84->32),
# ripup finishes to 0/0 (WL spent up to 69894 -- the healers' metrics don't
# track WL), and the trailing refine claws part of it back (69894->69621).
# The first refine doubles as a healer here BECAUSE the flow is healerless:
# its componentwise accept lets opens/overlap improvements through too.
source mix_tracks.buda
open_bdb mix2.bdb.sql
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
# NOTE: does NOT declare `set_planner_param healersAhead 1` (mix2.buda,
# its parent, does) even though it heals below.  Measured 2026-08-03:
# unlike its siblings, declaring would HOLD QoR (0/0/0) and IMPROVE
# detailed WL by 5.2% here — an open judgment call, not an oversight;
# left undeclared so the family stays consistent.  See
# docs/internal/wishlist-planner.md.
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
refine_selection
negotiate_congestion
ripup_reroute
# The trailing refine runs in `chase_overlaps` (plain lexicographic accept)
# rather than the default componentwise one — issue #535.  After the healers
# this flow stalls at ONE overlap whose only exit COSTS wirelength: refine's
# winning move is `bundle 62 topo 1->30`, ovl 1->0 at wl 68208->68509.  The
# default accept requires WL strictly lower with everything else parity-or-
# better, so it can never take that move no matter how many rounds run (a
# third and fourth round, and ripup budgets 30/60, were all measured
# byte-identical at 1 overlap), and ripup never reaches topo 30 either — its
# trial pool is contention-derived and screened, while refine sweeps every
# eligible bundle's alternates.  The plateau was a SEARCH-NEIGHBOURHOOD limit,
# not a budget or metric one.  Endpoint: 0/0/0, `check_design` Success, for
# +0.44% abstract WL (68200 -> 68500).
refine_selection 30 chase_overlaps
report_wl
check_design
exit
